lisa-design:
- Scheduled runs read repos.yaml in all six scheduled workflows; repos.mock.yaml stays a dispatch choice. Input default and the `inputs.manifest || ...` fallback are kept equal, as the workflows' own comments require.
- renovate.SelectRepos includes the kind-workflows repo by default (no special case left); named selection unchanged. compliance-framework/** packages stay disabled in the preset, so ccf-bump still owns internal pins (and the preset's non-api OPA rule leaves the workflows repo's OPA to ccf-bump as well).
- repos.mock.yaml also lists the workflows repo, so a default-repos mock dispatch of Renovate now reaches workflows too; docs/renovate.md says to pass -f repos=... to keep a mock run on the mocks only. Chosen over special-casing the mock manifest, which the spec did not ask for.
- vuln-summary and attention-digest CLIs now default --manifest to manifest.DefaultPath (repos.yaml), matching every other tool and the DefaultPath doc comment; the workflows always pass --manifest, so this changes no scheduled behaviour. vuln-summary's own SelectRepos still leaves workflows out by default (out of scope).
- No workflow is dispatched by this PR; it's a ci: change, so no workflows release.
